  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved knowledge and information base on the coverage and performance of social security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A major achievement resulting from ILO&#x2019;s support in the previous biennium was the comprehensive social protection reform in Oman that led to the ratification of an expansive new social protection law. It is expected to drive the modernization and redesign of the social protection system architecture in the Sultanate. Over the last 3 years, the ILO has provided technical assistance to Omani authorities on policy, legal, governance, actuarial, and socioeconomic modelling aspects of the reforms through a team of 10 specialized experts, coordinated by the ILO.  
Omani authorities indicated a strong will to continue with the unprecedented social protection reforms recently endorsed in the Sultanate . 
This biennium, ILO will build capacities and provide the necessary tools to enable the new institution to better assess the impact of social protection and enable a process of evidence-based policy making. A clear request was also made for ILO&#x2019;s technical support in the establishment of an actuarial unit and research unit and building their capacity.  ILO Technical support will also be provided to enable the ratification of the Social Security (Minimum Standards) Convention 102, in line with the unprecedented social security reforms being undertaken in Oman.  
 The ILO will also support the extension of key elements of the new social protection system to migrant workers, in line with the provisions of the new social protection law. This includes support in developing operational approaches for covering expats and engagement of countries of origin on possible coordination on social security.
In response to the interests expressed by the Omani authorities, the ILO will also provide technical support in carrying out a C183 legal gap analysis and in developing promotional material on the new maternity protection scheme for wider dissemination to the public.</narrative>
  </description>
